            <ArticleTitle>[Acute abdominal symptoms caused by segmental enteritis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1268-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical and anatomo-pathological patterns of Crohn's ileitis are reported and the various etiopathogenetic hypotheses are briefly considered. The acute forms of Crohn's ileitis are then described: appendicular, peritonitic, occlusive and toxic forms. The study is based on 68 personal cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
